SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE — READ THIS

The MIT license above covers ONLY the original material authored for this
repository: the packaging scripts, the launcher source, the icon generator, the
GitHub Actions workflows, and the documentation.

It does NOT cover RAPTOR itself, nor the third-party libraries bundled with it.

RAPTOR is third-party software redistributed here unmodified as part of a macOS
application bundle. It is **public domain**: the official project homepage
states that "the rest of RAPTOR, by US Air Force policy, is public domain", and
it was originally developed by and for the United States Air Force Academy.
Public domain imposes no conditions on redistribution; this project claims no
copyright in it.

The third-party libraries bundled alongside RAPTOR (Avalonia, SkiaSharp,
HarfBuzzSharp, libgdiplus and others) are NOT public domain and remain under
their own licences. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the full inventory.
